{"object":"A shutdown at a prescribed terminal-voltage floor even while significant capacity remains. The page does not quantify this worker's hidden charge under cold conditions.","predicate":"can_stop_with","source_url":"http://localhost:8090/content/wikipedia_en_all_nopic/Cutoff_voltage","subject":"phone cutoff voltage","text":"Cell phones can automatically shut down when cutoff voltage is reached, and a device can stop while significant battery capacity remains. Combined with the low-temperature voltage model, this explains why displayed charge need not equal usable cold power, but it does not reveal an exact hidden percentage for this phone.","title":"prop_phone_cutoff_remaining_capacity"}